WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.083
Welcome! In this video, we're going to be walking through exactly how discussion boards

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:10.217
work in our class, and also probably the same type of format for any

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:15.350
other class as well. So it's just making sure that you know how they

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.483
work, why we use them, and really, understanding how to get your full points

00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:21.950
for these discussion boards.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.419
And discussion boards really aren't just this busy work thing.

00:00:25.469 --> 00:00:28.889
They're where you get to see how your classmates think.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:33.746
You can learn from others, and be able to see the work that they're

00:00:33.796 --> 00:00:38.950
sharing, and then also be able to deepen your own understanding by explaining your reasoning.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.950
to others. So, it's a really great opportunity to make learning stick.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.750
Alright, so throughout this video, we're going to have different quick checks,

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.150
and you'll… the video will pause, it'll go to a little,

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.950
quiz question, and then you'll come back here, and it'll continue on.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.776
So, why are discussion boards a valuable part of this class?

00:01:01.826 --> 00:01:05.950
They let you see how classmates think and learn from their work.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.578
So every discussion board is going to follow the same three steps.

00:01:09.628 --> 00:01:12.299
First, you have to complete whatever the activity is.

00:01:12.349 --> 00:01:16.531
Sometimes it's going to be something where you create something and then upload an

00:01:16.581 --> 00:01:20.764
image of that thing. Sometimes it's just a discussion where you're doing a written

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:24.392
response. Okay, so depending on what it is, you'll do that first.

00:01:24.442 --> 00:01:26.810
Then you go ahead and post your work.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:31.950
So you're going to click the little reply button to make sure you post the work to

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.485
the assignment, and then, most importantly, the thing that most people always forget,

00:01:36.535 --> 00:01:39.624
is to come back and reply to two peers.

00:01:39.674 --> 00:01:44.508
Most often, it's two that I'm asking for, because then you can see different

00:01:44.558 --> 00:01:46.950
perspectives and see different types of work.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.458
So you have to come back in after other classmates have posted and reply

00:01:51.508 --> 00:01:55.967
to two people, and that third step is really kind of like a separate

00:01:56.017 --> 00:01:59.509
trip. You can't, necessarily finish it always the minute you post,

00:01:59.559 --> 00:02:03.374
so sometimes that's why we forget to go back and do it,

00:02:03.424 --> 00:02:05.950
but it is important for receiving full credit.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.950
Alright, on to a quick check.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.950
So, you've completed the activity and posted your work, what do you do next?

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.310
It is go back in and reply to at least two classmates.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.950
You're always welcome to do more, but usually I'm just asking for two.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.145
Now, let's talk about those replies.

00:02:25.195 --> 00:02:27.706
So those replies have to be thorough.

00:02:27.756 --> 00:02:31.730
I don't want to see just, I agree, or nice job,

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:37.950
or I did the same. One-liners on your discussion board replies will not get you full credit.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.394
Okay, so a full credit reply engages with your classmates and what they actually

00:02:43.444 --> 00:02:44.950
said, so you might

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.050
respond and, like, include what they said.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.250
You might add a point or ask a question to something that they said,

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.350
or connect it to your own work.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.950
But, like I said, just one-liners are not going to cut it.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:02.654
So when you go in, your discussion board, like, might look like something like

00:03:02.704 --> 00:03:07.950
this. You'll go in, you'll read what the prompt is, you'll click reply.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.200
And then you will go in and type your response,

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.450
or if it's a… an image you need to add,

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.000
you'll click this here and add an image, and then you… once you have

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.950
your full response, you'll click reply.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.236
Now, once you've gone in and done your initial post,

00:03:24.286 --> 00:03:27.193
then you need to reply to two other people.

00:03:27.243 --> 00:03:31.136
So this is just an example what the post might look like.

00:03:31.186 --> 00:03:35.736
You've done the thing, you've already replied, and now you need to go in

00:03:35.786 --> 00:03:40.336
and find two other students, click reply, and formulate a response to both of

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.307
them, using whatever the feedback was.

00:03:42.357 --> 00:03:43.950
So, for example, for my

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.950
post here, I tell you that your initial

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.768
post needs to be at least 100 words, and then you need to reply

00:03:51.818 --> 00:03:54.223
to two peers, with each reply containing 50 words.

00:03:54.273 --> 00:03:56.950
Sometimes I'll give you even, like, sentence starters for it,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.768
but you have to do your initial post first, and then you go in

00:04:00.818 --> 00:04:02.950
and find two other people to reply to.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.950
Alright, quick check.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.950
So, which reply would earn full credit?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.350
A reply that responds to the classmate's specific points and adds new… a new

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.807
idea or a question, is going to receive the full points.

00:04:19.857 --> 00:04:22.950
Remember, those one-liners are not going to work for me.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.450
Okay, so circling back to that idea again, two replies are required.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.700
So, it's the big one, really.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.950
If you post your own work.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.890
but then you never go back in and reply to two classmates,

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.860
you will not get full credit.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:42.457
So I need two thoughtful replies that show that you've engaged and read other

00:04:42.507 --> 00:04:47.054
people's work, and when I see it, if both of the replies are exactly

00:04:47.104 --> 00:04:51.323
the same, I'll ask you to go back and redo it as well,

00:04:51.373 --> 00:04:53.950
because the replies should be unique as well.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.950
Alright, quick check again.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.048
So what happens if you post your work, but never reply to two classmates?

00:05:03.098 --> 00:05:04.804
You will not receive full credit.

00:05:04.854 --> 00:05:08.316
It feels like I'm saying the same thing over and over again,

00:05:08.366 --> 00:05:10.950
but I'd want to make sure it's very clear.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.950
Alright, so one more important rule. So if…

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.850
you go back in and add replies after I've already graded the discussion.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:22.050
So if you go in, you see the work that you've gotten half points

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:25.050
on the assignment, I've left you a message and said,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:28.950
hey, you need to go back in and do the replies on this,

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.950
you can still do that, but it is very important.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.485
very, very important that you go in and you send me a message to

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:38.011
let me know it's complete. So once I've graded it,

00:05:38.061 --> 00:05:41.546
it shows as finished on my end, but I won't see your late replies

00:05:41.596 --> 00:05:45.081
unless you tell me, okay? It doesn't give me any alert anywhere that there's

00:05:45.131 --> 00:05:48.617
been a reply, so I need you to message me to let me know.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:52.152
And the way you message me is specific, so I'll show you what that

00:05:52.202 --> 00:05:54.677
looks like in a moment. It's not through Canvas Inbox,

00:05:54.727 --> 00:05:56.950
that makes it a lot harder on my end.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.950
So there's a really easy way.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.950
For you to message me, that'll get it right to the assignment.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.867
Alright, so here's what it looks like.

00:06:07.917 --> 00:06:09.950
If you have gone in.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.950
And you got that response that said, hey.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.683
I need you to go back in and do the replies for full credit.

00:06:15.733 --> 00:06:18.350
You will go in to… you can go through assignments,

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.817
you can go through Gradebook, and you're gonna go to the assignment again.

00:06:21.867 --> 00:06:25.550
You'll see what your initial response was, you'll see that there's no replies to

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.950
it, you'll have to open the discussion board again.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.709
And you'll have to go in and do the replies.

00:06:30.759 --> 00:06:33.743
And then after that, you need to come to assignments here,

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.950
find the assignment, and just add a comment.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.950
Okay, and in that comment, it should say.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.375
I have gone back in and replied to two peers.

00:06:42.425 --> 00:06:44.772
That's what the comment should say there.

00:06:44.822 --> 00:06:47.169
Press save, and that will notify me.

00:06:47.219 --> 00:06:51.621
Okay? So please don't go in to Canvas Inbox and do that message,

00:06:51.671 --> 00:06:56.416
because then it takes me 4 more steps to go back and grab the

00:06:56.466 --> 00:06:59.840
assignment. So you need to go in, grab the assignment,

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:03.950
add the message to the assignment itself after you've added the comments.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.950
Alright, quick check.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:11.450
So you finish your replies after your teacher already graded the discussion.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.950
What should you do?

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.500
Please go ahead and send your teacher a message that it's now complete,

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.950
and you saw how to do that.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.891
Alright, so just to kind of review discussion boards again,

00:07:22.941 --> 00:07:26.126
you're going to read the assignment, you're going to click reply,

00:07:26.176 --> 00:07:29.950
and then once you've clicked the reply, you're going to go ahead and

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.229
formulate your reply. Afterwards, make sure to click reply again,

00:07:33.279 --> 00:07:37.163
so it goes. And then afterwards, let me go back to this,

00:07:37.213 --> 00:07:41.425
you actually go ahead and when you go do your replies to students,

00:07:41.475 --> 00:07:45.032
it'll look like this, it'll be like someone's message, click reply,

00:07:45.082 --> 00:07:47.655
add the response here, and click reply again.

00:07:47.705 --> 00:07:49.950
So there's a lot of hitting reply.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:53.412
Okay? If you do not do the responses to peers,

00:07:53.462 --> 00:07:58.950
and they've already graded your work, then you need to make sure to go into Assignments.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:03.411
Grab that assignment, respond to two peers, and then go ahead and message me

00:08:03.461 --> 00:08:08.510
in the comments from assignments that I have gone back in and replied to two peers
